{"timestamp":"2026-05-06T17:30:23.419Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"exec_command_end","call_id":"call_esli01YxPAMNgHVLkoUbVFzj","process_id":"36492","turn_id":"019dfe56-9b4a-7e00-85f6-78c508241b46","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,220p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-06-lab-commands-design.md"],"cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-06-lab-commands-design.md","name":"2026-05-06-lab-commands-design.md","path":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-06-lab-commands-design.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Lab command discovery for experimental workflows\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-06\n**Status:** Draft - pending spec review and user review\n**Builds on:** PR #993 (`entire review`) and follow-up review refactor PRs #1105, #1106, #1107, #1111, #1112\n\n## Problem\n\n`entire review` is merged to `main`, but it is still a maturing workflow. We want users to discover it, try it, and understand that feedback may shape the final behavior. Keeping it completely hidden makes discovery poor; moving it under `entire lab review` creates a command path we may later need to undo, forcing early users to switch invocations when the command graduates.\n\nWe need a way to communicate \"this is available, experimental, and feedback-oriented\" while preserving the long-term command name:\n\n```text\nentire review\n```\n\n## Goals\n\n- Make experimental workflows discoverable through a visible top-level `lab` command.\n- Keep the stable user invocation unchanged from day one: `entire review`.\n- Give users clear expectations that lab commands may change based on feedback.\n- Avoid adding a mandatory lab flag or opt-in gate for non-destructive workflows.\n- Keep lab workflows out of the main top-level command list until they graduate.\n- Keep the implementation small enough to support additional lab commands later without building a full feature-flag framework.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not move `entire review` under `entire lab review` as the runnable command.\n- Do not require `--lab`, `--experimental`, config flags, or environment variables to run `entire review`.\n- Do not add telemetry, feedback submission, remote config, or release-channel behavior.\n- Do not define graduation policy in code. Promotion from lab to stable is a product/release decision.\n- Do not expose internal commands like hooks, migration, or telemetry through lab.\n\n## Design\n\n### Summary\n\nAdd a visible top-level informational command:\n\n```text\nentire lab\n```\n\n`entire lab` lists workflows that are available to try but still experimental. It does not become a runnable namespace. Lab entries point users to the canonical command path, for example:\n\n```text\nentire review\n```\n\n`entire review` remains the real command and stays hidden from root help while it is in lab. It is discoverable through `entire lab`, which lists the canonical invocation. Users call the same command path now that they will call after graduation.\n\n### User-facing behavior\n\nTop-level help includes a visible `lab` command:\n\n```text\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Manage agent integrations\n  checkpoint  Work with checkpoints\n  lab         Explore experimental Entire workflows\n```\n\n`review` does not appear in root help while it is in lab.\n\n`entire lab` prints an overview:\n\n```text\nLab commands\n\nThese are newer Entire workflows we are actively refining. They are available\nto try now, but details may change based on feedback.\n\nAvailable lab commands:\n  entire review    Run configured review skills against the current branch\n\nTry:\n  entire review --help\n```\n\n`entire lab review` is not part of v1. Lab is a listing/help surface only, not a command namespace and not a topic system. This avoids training users to invoke lab commands through a path that may disappear. Users who want command-specific detail should run the canonical command help:\n\n```text\nentire review --help\n```\n\n`entire review --help` includes the lab status in the long help:\n\n```text\nLab command: this workflow is experimental and may change based on feedback.\n```\n\nThe command itself should not print a warning on every run. Repeated warnings make normal use feel noisy. If extra caution is desired, limit it to first-run setup copy where the user is already making an explicit configuration choice.\n\n### Command model\n\nAdd a small lab metadata list in the CLI package:\n\n```go\ntype labCommandInfo struct {\n\tName       string\n\tInvocation string\n\tSummary    string\n}\n```\n\nInitial entries:\n\n```go\n{\n\tName:       \"review\",\n\tInvocation: \"entire review\",\n\tSummary:    \"Run configured review skills against the current branch\",\n}\n```\n\n`newLabCmd()` renders this list. Keeping the metadata separate from the Cobra command tree avoids needing to introspect command help, and gives future lab commands one clear place to opt in to the lab listing.\n\n`newLabCmd()` should support:\n\n- `entire lab`\n- `entire lab --help`\n\nIt should reject positional arguments.\n\nUnexpected positional argument:\n\n```text\nunknown lab topic \"review\"\n\nRun `entire lab` to see available lab commands, or run `entire review --help`\nfor command-specific help.\n```\n\nThe error should be non-silent and follow existing Cobra/main error handling unless a custom user-friendly message is printed, in which case use the local `SilentError` pattern.\n\n### `entire review` visibility\n\nKeep `review.NewCommand` hidden from root help while the workflow is in lab:\n\n```go\nHidden: true\n```\n\nThe command remains directly runnable as `entire review`. It is \"hidden from the root command list\", not disabled or private. There is no compatibility alias needed because the invocation does not change.\n\n### Help and docs\n\nUpdate docs and examples that mention the review workflow to use `entire review`, not `entire lab review`.\n\nAdd a small note in the review command long help:\n\n```text\nLab command: review is experimental. We are actively refining it based on user feedback.\n```\n\nAdd a short mention to README or the CLI command overview if that page lists discoverable top-level commands. If `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md` describe the review command as hidden, update them too. Avoid over-documenting lab policy until there is more than one lab command.\n\n## Error handling\n\n| Case | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `entire lab` has no registered lab commands | Print a friendly \"No lab commands are available in this build.\" message. |\n| `entire lab review` | Return a helpful error; do not run review. Point to `entire review --help`. |\n| `entire lab unknown` | Return an error with guidance to run `entire lab`. |\n| A lab metadata entry points to a command that is not registered | Unit tests should catch it. Runtime rendering can still list metadata because it is informational. |\n\n## Testing\n\n### Unit tests\n\nAdd tests around `newLabCmd()`:\n\n- `entire lab` prints the overview and includes `entire review`.\n- `entire lab --help` includes the lab overview or standard command help with the same intent.\n- `entire lab review` returns a helpful error and does not execute `entire review`.\n- `entire lab unknown` returns a helpful error.\n- The lab registry includes only commands that exist in the root command tree.\n\nAdd or update root command tests:\n\n- `entire review` remains hidden from root help while it is in lab.\n- `entire lab` is visible in root help.\n- Hidden infrastructure commands remain hidden.\n\nAdd review command tests:\n\n- `entire review --help` includes the lab status note.\n- `entire review` remains directly runnable even though it is hidden from root help.\n\n### Smoke verification\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run lint\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test.*(Lab|Review|Root)' -count=1\nmise run test:ci\n```\n\nBefore push, run the repository-required:\n\n```bash\nmise run lint\n```\n\n## Rollout\n\n1. Ship visible `entire lab` with hidden-from-root-help `entire review` listed inside it.\n2. Keep `entire review` as the only runnable path.\n3. Gather feedback from users running the review workflow.\n4. When the workflow graduates, unhide `review` in root help, remove the lab note from `review` help, and remove it from the lab metadata list. The invocation remains `entire review`, so no user migration is required.\n\n## Rejected approaches\n\n### Runnable namespace: `entire lab review`\n\nRejected because it creates a temporary command path. Users who adopt the lab form would later need to switch to `entire review`, which is exactly what we want to avoid.\n\n### Mandatory lab flag\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3417},"formatted_output":"","status":"completed"}}
