{"timestamp":"2026-05-06T21:38:47.516Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_y5LEcyVDQXRJjreIO1pySPKT","output":"Chunk ID: b1bd52\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 3064\nOutput:\n{\n  \"pull_request\": {\n    \"number\": 1132,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1132\",\n    \"title\": \"fix(review): include checkpoint context in prompts\",\n    \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n    \"owner\": \"entireio\",\n    \"repo\": \"cli\"\n  },\n  \"conversation_comments\": [],\n  \"reviews\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRR_kwDOQyo98M78scny\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nThis PR enhances `entire review` prompt generation by appending compact, best-effort checkpoint-derived context for commits within the detected review scope, so reviewers can reference relevant checkpoint IDs and summaries without inlining raw transcripts.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Add `CheckpointContext` to review run configuration and append it to composed prompts (while keeping `PromptOverride` verbatim).\\n- Introduce checkpoint-context extraction for the review scope, preferring checkpoint summaries and falling back to stored prompts, with guidance to use `entire explain` for full context.\\n- Wire the new context provider through dependency injection and add unit/smoke tests covering prompt composition and end-to-end prompt capture for a stubbed agent.\\n\\n### Reviewed changes\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 9 out of 9 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n\\n| File | Description |\\r\\n| ---- | ----------- |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go | Extends review run configuration with checkpoint context. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go | Updates nolint rationale comments for Bubble Tea interface returns. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt.go | Appends checkpoint context to generated prompts (non-override path). |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt_test.go | Adds coverage ensuring checkpoint context is included and override remains verbatim. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go | Injects and threads checkpoint context into single- and multi-agent run configs. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd_test.go | Adjusts stub reviewer `Start` signature to match interface usage style. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review_context.go | Implements best-effort checkpoint context extraction for a scoped range of commits. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review_context_test.go | Adds tests for summary/prompt fallback behavior and a smoke test verifying prompt inclusion. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review_bridge.go | Wires the checkpoint-context provider into review deps from the CLI package. |\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:56:35Z\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRR_kwDOQyo98M78seQq\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW -->\\nCursor Bugbot has reviewed your changes and found 1 potential issue.\\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_FIX_ALL -->\\n<a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix All in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"></picture></a>\\n<!-- /BUGBOT_FIX_ALL -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_AUTOFIX_REVIEW_FOOTNOTE_BEGIN -->\\n<sup>\\u274c Bugbot Autofix is OFF. To automatically fix reported issues with cloud agents, enable autofix in the [Cursor dashboard](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- BUGBOT_AUTOFIX_REVIEW_FOOTNOTE_END -->\\n\\n_Comment `@cursor review` or `bugbot run` to trigger another review on this PR_\\n\\n\\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 0c630e2ce8350f58396a26f728cf22df1e6a36a7. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:57:44Z\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"cursor\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"review_threads\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6AILoA\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/review_context.go\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"diffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"startLine\": null,\n      \"startDiffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"originalLine\": 60,\n      \"originalStartLine\": 37,\n      \"resolvedBy\": null,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M6-lShw\",\n            \"body\": \"`reviewCheckpointContext` builds context by listing every commit in the scope and then running `git show` once per commit. This is O(N) process spawns and can noticeably slow `entire review` on large branches; it also makes it hard to keep the generated prompt compact. Consider switching to a single `git log <range> --format=...` call that yields commit messages in one invocation (or otherwise batching) and enforcing a hard cap on how many commits/checkpoints are scanned.\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:56:34Z\",\n            \"updatedAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:56:35Z\",\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6AILoR\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/review_context.go\",\n      \"line\": 91,\n      \"diffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"startLine\": 57,\n      \"startDiffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"originalLine\": 77,\n      \"originalStartLine\": 57,\n      \"resolvedBy\": null,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M6-lSiF\",\n            \"body\": \"The checkpoint context has a per-item truncation limit, but there\\u2019s no overall cap on how many checkpoint lines can be appended to the review prompt. On a branch with many checkpointed commits this can still blow up prompt size (tokens) and hurt both latency and quality. Consider enforcing a maximum number of checkpoints/lines (and indicating when output is truncated).\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:56:35Z\",\n            \"updatedAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:56:35Z\",\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6AILod\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/review_context.go\",\n      \"line\": 133,\n      \"diffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"startLine\": 93,\n      \"startDiffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"originalLine\": 113,\n      \"originalStartLine\": 93,\n      \"resolvedBy\": null,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M6-lSiW\",\n            \"body\": \"`reviewCheckpointDetail` calls `readReviewContextSessionMetadata` for each session twice (once in the summary pass, again in the prompt fallback pass). If the underlying reader falls back to `ReadSessionContent`, this can duplicate I/O and parsing work per checkpoint. Consider reading metadata once per session (cache results) or combining the summary/prompt selection into a single pass.\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:56:35Z\",\n            \"updatedAt\": \"2026-05-06T20:56:35Z\",\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"